A highlighter port is an interface for highlighting code, independent of the chosen highlighting tool.
This follows [ports and adapters](/lore/hexagonal-architecture).

The [code-snippets design brief](/lore/code-snippets) specifies an engine-neutral token:
- `text`: token source text.
- `role`: syntax role.
- `fontStyle`: style information.

The highlighter port also exposes languages, aliases, themes, and an engine fingerprint.
This identifier records the highlighter, version, and settings used in token cache keys.

The proposed Shiki adapter keeps Shiki's token type inside the adapter.
A plain adapter returns uncoloured text.
Both adapters provide the same port through an [Effect Layer](/lore/layer-constructor-pattern).

Core properties use the plain adapter.
The whole-file token property exercises Shiki.
[One snippet model](/lore/one-snippet-model-two-renderers) supplies both renderers.

See [the glossary](/glossary) for engine-neutral token and highlighter port.
